  "name": "Fibrinogen ",
  "code": "FIB",
  "cost": 0,
  "interpretation": "<table><thead><tr><th><div>Fibrinogen Level</div></th><th><div>Interpretation</div></th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><div>Below Normal Range</div></td><td><div>Reduced fibrinogen levels may indicate fibrinogen deficiency or consumption, which can occur in conditions such as disseminated intravascular coagulation (DIC) or liver disease. Further evaluation and appropriate management are needed.</div></td></tr><tr><td><div>Normal Range</div></td><td><div>Fibrinogen levels within the normal range suggest adequate fibrinogen production and function.</div></td></tr><tr><td><div>Above Normal Range</div></td><td><div>Elevated fibrinogen levels may be seen in acute inflammatory conditions, such as infection or tissue injury, as part of the acute-phase response. It may also occur in conditions like pregnancy or certain cancers. Clinical correlation is necessary to determine the underlying cause.</div></td></tr></tbody></table>",
